        "created_at": "2024-03-18T12:44:06.446Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So I have tried to find answers for this by scouring the rulebook, various forums, wikis, and FAQs. But it’s such a simple question that it’s difficult to search for! I think I have it right, but I want to double check.</p>\n<p>Some actions, like Push, can either read “Push 3 Dahan” or “Push up to 3 Dahan”.</p>\n<p>So for the first example, that must mean that you <strong>have</strong> to push 3, whether you like it or not? At least, that’s my conclusion.</p>\n<p>Second, I assume based on the <em>do as much as you can</em> principle that I can still target a land that has <em>fewer</em> than 3 Dahan with that power? Or does the effect <strong>require</strong> 3 Dahan to be present?</p>\n<p>Grateful for any help!</p>\n<p>And thanks for an awesome game, so happy I discovered it. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"></p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2024-03-18T12:44:06.446Z",
        "reply_count": 1,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 140,
